    "noteZh": "以色列人讲究“dugri”——有话直说。反馈直接、争论大声、插话代表投入，而且都不针对个人：上午十点跟你吵得面红耳赤的人，晚上六点可能就请你去家里吃安息日晚餐。层级出奇地扁平——初级工程师敢当面质疑CEO——“chutzpah”（大胆闯劲）在这里是句夸人的话。",
    "noteEn": "Israelis practice \"dugri\"—straight talk. Feedback is blunt, debate is loud, interrupting signals engagement, and none of it is personal: the person arguing fiercely with you at 10 a.m. may invite you to Shabbat dinner at 6 p.m. Hierarchy is remarkably flat—junior engineers challenge CEOs to their faces—and chutzpah, audacious initiative, is a compliment.",
